Appendix G. Formal Specification Sketch in TLA⁺ for P1–P3c

The following is a specification sketch, not a verified module. It illustrates the intended linearization semantics and the separation of P3a, P3b, and P3c. The full module is declared as planned work (Open Problem 4).

G.1 State variables

```
VARIABLES
    monitor_state,      \* S_monitor
    history,            \* h_t
    committed,          \* set of committed operation ids
    revoked,            \* set of revoked delegation ids
    admitted            \* set of admitted (checked but not yet committed) ops
```

G.2 Authorization action

```
Permit(a) ==
    /\ a \in EffectiveActions(monitor_state)
    /\ ContextSatisfied(a, monitor_state)
    /\ BudgetSufficient(a, monitor_state)
    /\ ~InForbidden(history, a)
    /\ ~BlockedByRevocation(a, revoked)
```

G.3 Check action (P3a linearization point)

```
Check(a) ==
    /\ Permit(a)
    /\ admitted' = admitted \cup {opid(a)}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<monitor_state, history, committed, revoked>>
```

G.4 Commit action

```
Commit(a) ==
    /\ opid(a) \in admitted
    /\ ~BlockedByRevocation(a, revoked)      \* P3a: re-check at commit
    /\ committed' = committed \cup {opid(a)}
    /\ admitted' = admitted \ {opid(a)}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<monitor_state, history, revoked>>
```

G.5 At-most-once delivery (P3b)

```
AtMostOnce ==
    \A a1, a2 :
        (Committed(a1) /\ Committed(a2) /\
         opid(a1) = opid(a2) /\ recv(a1) = recv(a2)) =>
        a1 = a2
```

G.6 Revocation semantics (P3c)

Three variants, each declared before verification:

```
P3c_BlockUncommitted ==
    \A a : Revoked(a) => ~Committed(a)

P3c_AffectCommitted ==
    \A a : Revoked(a) => (Committed(a) => Compensate(a))

P3c_Both ==
    P3c_BlockUncommitted /\ P3c_AffectCommitted
```

G.7 Theorem obligations

The following are obligations to be discharged in the full module:

· P1. For every executed action $a$, Permit(a) was evaluated at some prior state.
· P3a. For every commit, there exists a check with $t_{\text{check}} < t_{\text{commit}}$ and no intervening revocation that invalidates Permit.
· P3b. AtMostOnce is an invariant.
· P3c. The chosen variant is an invariant under the declared revocation model.

